        <span class="eyebrow on-dark">The Programme Thesis</span>
        <h2 class="h2">Five critical themes<br/>for 2027.</h2>
        <p class="lede on-dark">Every session at RegSymp maps to one of five themes that the programme committee has identified as the most consequential regulatory and operational shifts facing major financial institutions over the next 24 months.</p>
      </div>

      <ol class="themes-list" aria-label="Programme themes">
        <li class="theme-row"><span class="num">01</span><div><h3 class="theme-title">The Future of European Finance</h3><p>Can Europe lead the next era of financial innovation across banking, payments, AI and digital assets while remaining globally competitive?</p></div></li>
        <li class="theme-row"><span class="num">02</span><div><h3 class="theme-title">Payments, Stablecoins &amp; Programmable Money</h3><p>How embedded finance, stablecoins, tokenisation and next-generation payment infrastructure are reshaping the movement of money.</p></div></li>
        <li class="theme-row"><span class="num">03</span><div><h3 class="theme-title">AI, Wealth &amp; The Reinvention of Banking</h3><p>Exploring whether AI will transform — or replace — traditional banking, wealth management and private banking models.</p></div></li>
        <li class="theme-row"><span class="num">04</span><div><h3 class="theme-title">Trust, Infrastructure &amp; Institutional Resilience</h3><p>The operational backbone behind modern finance: custody, safeguarding, operational resilience, cybersecurity and scalable infrastructure.</p></div></li>
        <li class="theme-row"><span class="num">05</span><div><h3 class="theme-title">The New Financial Ecosystem</h3><p>How banks, fintechs, family offices, digital asset firms, investors and technology leaders are converging to build the next generation of financial services.</p></div></li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="attendee-block">
      <div class="attendee-grid">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow on-dark">Who Should Attend</span>
          <h3 class="h2" style="font-size:clamp(28px,3vw,40px); margin-bottom:14px;">A room of peers.</h3>
          <p class="lede on-dark">RegSymp is designed for the people who actually own the regulatory outcomes inside major financial institutions.</p>
          <p class="role-list"><em>CEOs, Founders, CROs, COOs, Chief Compliance Officers, MLROs, General Counsel, Heads of Custody, Heads of Operational Resilience, Internal Audit Partners, Regulatory Advisors and Big 4 Partners.</em></p>
